[]},{"date":"2019-12-24T12:33:26-08:00","id":1356839,"title":"","content":"I've got a whole mess of them that I will try to post later. The one that I just used last session were &quot;Eagle Cherries&quot;. When eaten in pairs, both consumers are lost in dance and spend the next 5 min moving to whatever music that is in their heart. Upon finishing their dance, the pair will have swapped their worst memories (get it... Eagles... some dance to remember, some dance to forget).<br /> <br /> Definitely not one that the players should have regular access to, but makes a great little plot hook when the characters stumble upon a Satyr EDM rave in the Hedge. With a Centaur DJ.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24245-ruggedrock","name":"ruggedrock","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-24T13:21:22-08:00","id":1356848,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ruggedrock</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1353601-homebrew-goblin-fruit?p=1356839#post1356839\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've got a whole mess of them that I will try to post later. The one that I just used last session were &quot;Eagle Cherries&quot;. When eaten in pairs, both consumers are lost in dance and spend the next 5 min moving to whatever music that is in their heart. Upon finishing their dance, the pair will have swapped their worst memories (get it... Eagles... some dance to remember, some dance to forget).<br /> <br /> Definitely not one that the players should have regular access to, but makes a great little plot hook when the characters stumble upon a Satyr EDM rave in the Hedge. With a Centaur DJ.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oooh! Not a bad one at all! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-24T15:04:55-08:00","id":1356855,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ruggedrock</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1353601-homebrew-goblin-fruit?p=1356839#post1356839\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've got a whole mess of them that I will try to post later. The one that I just used last session were &quot;Eagle Cherries&quot;. When eaten in pairs, both consumers are lost in dance and spend the next 5 min moving to whatever music that is in their heart. Upon finishing their dance, the pair will have swapped their worst memories (get it... Eagles... some dance to remember, some dance to forget).</div> </div> </div> </div>I read that as &quot;Eagle Eye Cherries&quot; at first..I don't know if anyone else remembers this band, they only had like one hit in the US.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>When the cat's a Stray, the mice will pray...</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25851-thestray7","name":"TheStray7","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25851_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"176"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-24T19:56:28-08:00","id":1356890,"title":"","content":"It is a staple of rock radio to this day though","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-25T08:10:28-08:00","id":1356926,"title":"","content":"Here are a few more goblin fruit/oddments that I've set up...<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Roboto\"> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">Transmission Trees</span><br /> </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Roboto\"> <br /> <br /> The trees in the grove look like transmission towers, tall, with blinking red lights at the top. If one were to climb to the top of one of these trees, they would find that the glowing lights are bulbs, filled with flat 1 cm square seed (they look like micro chips).<br /> <br /> If one were to stick one of these &quot;chips&quot; behind their ear before they drift off to sleep, they would gain the following traits through the night...<br /> - Perfect recollection of all their dreams<br /> - 9 Again on Favoured Regalia Contracts<br /> - +1 Composure Defense against Oneirmancy shifts<br /> - No willpower regained from rest<br /> <br /> </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Roboto\"> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">Sappy Trees</span><br /> </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Roboto\"> <br /> <br /> This wood has trees that can be tapped for a salty liquid. Once this sap is procured and boiled down, it can be drunk. It has a nutty aroma, and tastes like what one would think Pine Sol tastes like. <br /> <br /> Gain 1 Glamour and immediately recover from any level of inebriation one may be at. Note, this can counter the effect of pain meds, causing more harm than good.<br /> <br /> </span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Roboto\"> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">The Swamp</span><br /> </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Roboto\"> <br /> <br /> The Cattails in this swamp end in small, fuzzy seeds. If one is able to keep one of these under their tongue until it dissolves (about 5 minutes), they would find their heart burn cured for a day, as well as the normal glamour gain<br /> <br /> </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Roboto\"> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">The Marsh</span><br /> </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Roboto\"> <br /> <br /> This marshland is a favourite of amphibious minded hedge creatures, with Briar Salamanders prevalent in the shallow pools.<br /> <br /> The bullrushes here grow with a viscous liquid the colour of ash along their stocks. Anyone who applies this liquid on their bodies gain +1 natural armour for a scene. However, anyone who doesn't wash it off afterwards will have inverted colour vision until they do.<br /> <br /> </span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24245-ruggedrock","name":"ruggedrock","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-25T09:36:50-08:00","id":1356931,"title":"","content":"So, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24245-ruggedrock\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24245\" data-vbnamecard=\"24245\">ruggedrock</a> , two questions about the marshland bullrushes. Is that armor boost to general or ballistic? and how are the colors inverted? that can mean different things depending on which color wheel you are using? Did you mean everything looks like a photonegative?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":7920,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","user":"Master Aquatosic","date":". 12-25-2019, 12:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-25T10:21:54-08:00","id":1356933,"title":"","content":"<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode__table--wrapper text_table_\"><table class=\"b-bbcode__table text_table\"><tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Is that armor boost to general or ballistic? and how are the colors inverted? that can mean different things depending on which color wheel you are using? Did you mean everything looks like a photonegative? </div> </div> </div></td> </tr> </table></div> I'm not one to answer these questions, that is up for the GM to determine /sarcasm<br /> <br /> I'd imagine there armour would be 1/1, however I could see it being 1/0. Its magic war paint after all, what suits the story better?<br /> <br /> For the inverted colours, I intended this to be incredibly thematic, and hadn't nailed down any mechanical repercussions, outside of a general negative to perception. I mostly envisioned that standard colour wheel, just so I didn't have to deal with potential night-vision abuses. I would describe things like &quot;deep orange sky, purple sun&quot; and &quot;red grass and purple soil&quot;. However, the photo negative angle sounds cool. All the power if you can make it work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24245-ruggedrock","name":"ruggedrock","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}